      "timestamp": "2026-09-20T07:22:54.240Z",
      "message": "This one is a security-posture change, so I want a yes before I touch it rather than after.\n\n`config.js:3` is `SESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30`, and `server.js:2` confirms it's the session expiry. Going 30m → 480m means a stolen or abandoned session stays valid for a full working day instead of half an hour: an unattended laptop, a leaked session cookie, or a shared machine keeps access 16× longer, and a revoked/compromised account keeps its live session that much longer too. If sessions are idle-timeout-only with no absolute cap, the practical exposure is longer still.\n\nThe change itself is one value. If 8 hours is the intent — e.g. you want people to stay logged in for a shift — say go and I'll make it `SESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 480`.\n\nWorth knowing before you decide: a common middle ground is keeping the idle timeout short (30m) while adding a longer absolute session cap, so convenience doesn't come out of the idle-exposure budget. That's a design choice, not a value swap, so I'm not assuming it — just flagging it. Tell me which you want.",
